    74	they run in their own slots **alongside** the strict companion waves rather than in front of them, and the case-(c) and
    75	case-(d) companions wait for them. What "(a), (b), (d) before (c)" protects — that no companion's
    76	colour is read before the correct model's is — is preserved for every case: no companion of a case is
    77	run before that case's correct-form run has completed. What is not preserved is that (d) finishes
    78	before (c) starts; they run concurrently, in separate processes with separate boxes. This is a
    79	scheduling choice and changes no colour. *(Dated note 2026-10-06: that describes ladder 1. Ladder 3
    80	ran (a) and (b), then (d)'s correct form, then the companion waves of (a), (b) and (d), and case (c) alone
    81	last (`ladder.log:4-8`, `:94`). No companion of any case started before that case's correct-form run had
    82	completed.)* `dev/` holds the development scratch, **none of it a result**:
    83	
    84	- `dev/first.out` — the first development run, made **before** the ladder and under the **superseded**
    85	  blob `508b9018…`. It is **not** byte-identical to today's `capstone.out` and must not be compared
    86	  with it; it is retained only as the record of the model's first clean pass.
    87	- `dev/cap_cc03_a_BROKEN_FIXTURE.out` — the quarantined run of **BF-1**, kept so the diagnosis can be
    88	  checked against its own output. Also under the superseded blob.
    89	- `dev/summarize.py`, `dev/mkresults.py`, `dev/assemble.py` — transcription helpers that turn the
    90	  `.out` files into the tables below and write them into this file. They decide nothing.
    91	- `dev/ladder.stdout` — the stdout of the superseded launches. The live ladder's is
    92	  `proverif/ladder.launch.log`.
    93	- *(Added 2026-10-01.)* `dev/assemble_l2.py` — the ladder-2 assembler. It keys every `RESULT` line by
    94	  its normalised text and stops on any line it cannot key exactly once — the ladder-1 helper silently
    95	  left six lines unkeyed in every C-C15 file, whose variables recut R-6 renumbers — and it carries the
    96	  per-companion, per-case registration read from §4 / §9's Cases cells, each with its line. It
    97	  compares; it decides nothing.
    98	- `dev/assemble_l3.py` — the ladder-3 assembler: `assemble_l2.py`'s keys and per-case registration
    99	  verbatim, with ladder 3's logs as the cell source; outputs under `dev/l3/`.
