   104	
   105	**TWO READINGS OF THE COMPANION BOX, AND WHICH ONE THIS FILE REPORTS UNDER.** The registration can
   106	be read two ways on how much wall clock a companion is allowed, and the cross-family reviewer will
   107	ask which governs, so both are recorded for every companion run and neither is decided here. *(REPAIR
   108	2026-10-01, skeptic S-4: the choice is now routed to the author, with its effect row by row; see section 3,
   109	*Which box reading each severing depends on*, and *ROUTED TO THE AUTHOR — second question*.)*
   110	
   111	- **The per-case-sum reading.** §3's timebox table declares a box per registered query and totals
   112	  them: *"**Total declared, per compromise case** | | **27** | **1185 min (19 h 45 m)**"*
   113	  (`:1595`), with the whole-ladder ceiling *"at most **4 × 1185 = 4740 min (79 h)**"* (`:1599`,
   114	  `:1620`). Each `.pv` here carries **every** registered query of its case, so on this reading a run
   115	  is allowed the sum of the boxes of the queries it carries — 1185 min for a strict case, 1095 min
   116	  for (d), which asserts neither link 1b nor C-Q2. **`run_ladder.sh` enforces this reading**, because
   117	  it is the one a single file carrying every query can be held to.
   118	- **The predicted-red reading.** §4's count paragraph says *"**No companion carries a timebox**:
   119	  §3's timebox table is over registered **queries** only, and **a companion runs inside the box of
   120	  the query it is predicted to red**"* (`:1867-1870`), with the per-companion assignments spelled out
   121	  where they are not obvious — *"C-C17 runs inside link 2a's 45-minute box"* and *"C-C16 runs inside
   122	  link 5's 60-minute box"* (`:1873-1875`), *"C-C18 runs inside C-Q10's 30-minute box"* (`:1875-1876`),
   123	  C-C8's isolation runs *"inside C-Q9's 60-minute box"* (§9(2)). On this reading a companion's box is
   124	  30 to 90 minutes, not 1185.
   125	
   126	Section 2 therefore carries **two columns**: `rc` and seconds under the per-case-sum box the ladder
   127	actually enforced, and whether that same run finished inside the box of the query it is predicted to
   128	red. Where a companion is predicted to red more than one query the **strictest** reading is taken —
   129	the **smallest** of their boxes — and the column names which query it is. **Nothing is re-run to
   130	produce this**: both columns are read off the one `ladder.log` line. If the strict reading governs,
   131	section 2's second column is the report under it; if the per-case-sum reading governs, the first
   132	column is.
   133	
   134	*(REPAIR 2026-10-01, skeptic S-10.)* Where the registration **assigns** a companion's box in words, section
   135	2's column does not use it: it takes the smallest box among the companion's predicted-red queries, 30
   136	minutes, for three companions the registration assigns elsewhere — C-C17 to link 2a's 45-minute box, C-C16 to
   137	link 5's 60-minute box, and C-C9 to link 2b's, which is 60 minutes (`PREDICTIONS.md:1873-1875`; §3's table,
   138	`:1588`). **No yes/no changes**, checked run by run on ladder 3: C-C9 ran 240, 246 and 1 323 s, inside both 30 and 60
   139	minutes; C-C16 ran 275 and 251 s in strict (inside both) and 6 261 s in (d) (outside both); C-C17 ran
   140	27 085 and 25 996 s (outside both). The generated column is therefore left as it is. Which reading governs
   141	at all is routed to the author (*ROUTED TO THE AUTHOR — second question*), and the row-by-row effect is in
   142	section 3 (*Which box reading each severing depends on*).
   143	
   144	**The whole-ladder ceiling.** §3 puts it at *"at most 4 × 1185 = 4740 min (79 h)"* (`:1620`). The
   145	ladder's total wall clock against that ceiling is recorded under **Not run** when it completes, and
   146	if it exceeds the ceiling this file says so plainly.
   147	
   148	**Timeboxes, and how they are read here.** §3's table declares a box **per registered query**, 27
   149	entries and 1185 min per compromise case. Each `.pv` here carries **every** registered query of its
   150	case, so each run is given the **per-case sum**: 1185 min for a strict case, 1095 min for (d), which
   151	asserts neither link 1b nor C-Q2. Because a whole-model run's wall clock is an upper bound on every
   152	query's own time, **a run that finishes under 30 minutes is inside the smallest registered box for
   153	every query it carries**; `ladder.log` records the seconds so that can be checked rather than taken
   154	on trust. No companion carries a box of its own (§4, "The count"); it runs inside the box of the
   155	query it is predicted to red, and a fortiori inside the sum.
