   303	- *Preservation.* A later renewal wraps a V1 receipt and never alters its verdict (R-1.18, P7). A later degraded policy never changes a strict verdict whose evidence is all present.
   304	- *Evidence for preservation.* Both are tested with `G_v1` as in A9.4 (i), together with the A6.1 vector once wrapping exists.
   305	- *Custody.* Until renewal exists, a V1 receipt's long-horizon validity depends on ECDSA P-256 and SHA-256 surviving, and on the holder keeping the bundle. The relying-party story says so.
