    45	## 0. What was built, and how the other files are derived
    46	
    47	`capstone.pv` is **the** composed model, in case **(a)** — strict, DNS channel compromised. It carries
    48	the §1.1 fixture, the §1.2 acceptance path per layer, the §1.3 events, and **every** registered query
    49	of that case in one file. The other cases and every companion are **derived from it** by
    50	`formal/suite/capstone/proverif/derive.py`, which applies named, exact-string edits inside named
    51	blocks of the model and writes a header into each generated file naming its case, what it mutates,
    52	which registered prediction it serves and the registered box. Nothing in `derive.py` edits
    53	`capstone.pv`. The delta for any generated file is therefore readable twice: in `derive.py`'s rule
    54	list, and as `diff capstone.pv <file>`.
    55	
    56	- **(a)** strict, `skD` public — `capstone.pv` itself (no copy: the file the registration names is the
    57	  file that runs, so the blob hash is its own).
    58	- **(b)** strict, `skR` public — `capstone_b.pv`, one line.
    59	- **(c)** strict, **both** channel keys public — `cap_cc01_c.pv`, one line. Per §1.1's cases table
    60	  this case **is** companion **C-C1**, not a correct-form run.
    61	- **(d)** degraded, sole channel public — `capstone_d.pv`, a **documented copy**: `derive.py`'s
    62	  `degraded()` transformation and nothing else (one authority channel; one evidence check; `ev` the
    63	  sole term rather than §1.3's pair; `AcceptS` in place of the library's `Accept`; **C-Q1 link 1b and
    64	  C-Q2 not asserted**, per §1.1's cases table and §3; **C-Q6 conjunct 1's unrestricted form not
    65	  asserted**, per §3 §(5)).
    66	
    67	`run_ladder.sh` runs the ladder in the registered order (§3), with one departure that is stated
    68	rather than taken silently. The registered order is *"C-Q1's links before every companion; (a), (b),
    69	(d) before (c); C-Q7, C-Q8, C-Q9 before links 3 and 4 and before C-Q6"* (`:301-304`). The last clause
    70	is a **query** order and is honoured by the declaration order inside `capstone.pv`. The first is a
    71	**run** order and is honoured: the case-(a) and case-(b) correct-form runs are a barrier and complete
    72	before any companion starts. **The departure:** cases (c) and (d) are materially more expensive than the
    73	strict correct-form cases — by a factor not yet measured under the repaired model (finding F-3) — so
    74	they run in their own slots **alongside** the strict companion waves rather than in front of them, and the case-(c) and
    75	case-(d) companions wait for them. What "(a), (b), (d) before (c)" protects — that no companion's
    76	colour is read before the correct model's is — is preserved for every case: no companion of a case is
    77	run before that case's correct-form run has completed. What is not preserved is that (d) finishes
    78	before (c) starts; they run concurrently, in separate processes with separate boxes. This is a
